# T-E5-003 — E5 decision source

The owner approved a separate E5 prerequisite after PR #3's narrow remediation review. This task builds a current PostgreSQL decision source from session, grant, actor-epoch and policy rows, with no stored ALLOW result. An independent T3 second-eye review approved PR #4 only for that decision-source slice. It does not activate privileged production, create a provider account, or complete T-E3-001-R1. At that review, identity writers and E3's trusted resource read and real product mutation in the same transaction, plus audit and negative-floor sources, were missing; status stays IN_PROGRESS.

The candidate in `[[vault/PACKS/P-E3-001-R3.md]]` adds a public E5 consumer authority surface, Supabase Auth verification and provider-session locking, and trusted one-time consumer enrollment/session writers. Its local integration test binds the E5 decision to E3's maintenance transaction. This is a candidate awaiting independent task-level review; hosted production activation and privileged identity flows are not proved. T-E5-003 stays IN_PROGRESS.
